The "Darmok" episode of Star Trek : TNG.  The aliens du jour spoke entirely
in terms of well-known events in their culture, i.e., "the river mumble in
winter" meant "stop" because the river stopped (froze); to speak of a
current behavior they would refer to a person who was known for that
behavior, etc.  Without being a historian of that culture, it was difficult
to tell what they meant, even with the Amazing Universal Translator (TM)
engaged.  It could have been really interesting if the story didn't have to
be collapsed into 42 minutes of TV, requiring oversimplification of the
clues that allowed Captain Picard to start understanding them.

